window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>When Reyes Moreno is forced to come back to his childhood town after being exiled for twenty-one years, the last thing he’s expecting is to be dragged into a murder to clear his brother’s name. Much less is he expecting to have to solve it with his old high school friend-turned-enemy, Zachary Becker.</p> <p></p> <p>Determined to prove his brother’s innocence, Reyes tries to ignore the ghosts of his past that are determined to haunt him. More importantly, he’s trying to ignore that old flame that, even after two decades, still burns brightly for his arch enemy.</p> <p></p> <p>Can you solve an impossible string of murders in a town that hates you?</p> <p></p> <p>Can you try not to fall in love with the same guy twenty-one years later?</p> <p></p> <p>Anything is possible in Willow Falls.</p>"; 
